 "notes": "A lilting 6/8 tide that starts below the home note, on the sixth, climbs by step to the third and holds it a whole bar, then slips down past the start to the fifth below. A little wistful; it begins on the minor chord. Winter: D minor, the theme in augmentation over open fifths, a bowed high line, and an inverted fragment to close."
